brunor: Percy! What a surprise! I thought you'd left us all behind. How's life on the outside?
- It's alright
	brunor: Just alright?
- Better than being stuck inside
	brunor: You’ve got that right.
brunor: I hear you’ve got so many new things out there. Like the internet! His Highness only lets us have phones, and even then just barely.
- His Highness
	brunor: Yes, King Arthur remains in power, though I suppose he’s the hotel manager now and all of us, his workers. Just as well you failed to join the Round Table, Percy. I would’ve liked to roam around the greater world and see it all change, but no, us proper knights are stuck in here.
	- Stuck?
		brunor: Yes, stuck. Mind you, I'd be here anyway. I've reason to believe [b]my father's murderer[/b] is still here, and I've sworn on his coat that I won't even let his spirit rest!
- Phones
	brunor: Phones, yes, we've phones, and elevators. Electricity is a marvelous thing, isn't it, Percy?
	- Elevators
		brunor: Yes, two guest elevators and a staff elevator. I can't let you use the staff elevator, though, sorry Percy. You're not staff, after all.